===============================================================================
DB2 interactive Call Level Interface (CLI) environment - writecfg mode
===============================================================================

You can use the DB2 interactive CLI environment in writecfg mode to perform the
following task (s):

  - Add or Remove dsn entry in the db2dsdriver.cfg file.
  - Add or Remove database entry in the dsdriver.cfg file.
  - Add, Modify or Remove parameters in the db2dsdriver.cfg file.
  - Add, Modify or Remove session global variables in the db2dsdriver.cfg file.
  - Add, Modify or Remove special registers in the db2dsdriver.cfg file.
  - Add, Modify or Remove ACR parameters in the db2dsdriver.cfg file.
  - Add, Modify or Remove ACR subsections like alternategroup,
    alternateserverlist, affinitylist, clientaffinitydefined,
    clientaffinityroundrobin.
  - Add, Modify or Remove WLB parameters in the db2dsdriver.cfg file.

Command syntax

  db2cli writecfg
      {
        add    { [ [-dsn <dsn_name> -description <dsn_description>]
                   -database <dbname> -host <server> -port <port> ],
                 [ [-parameter[s] "<par1>=<val1>
                                   [;...;<parN>=<valN>;]"]
                   [-sessionglobalvariables "<par1>=<val1>
                                             [;...;<parN>=<valN>;]"]
                   [-specialregisters "<par1>=<val1>
                                       [;...;<parN>=<valN>;]"]
                   [-wlb "[<par1>=<val1>;...;<parN>=<valN>;]"]
                   [-acr "[<par1>=<val1>;...;<parN>=<valN>;]"
                      [-alternategroup "[<par1>=<val1>;...;<parN>=<valN>;]"
                           -database <dbname> -host <server> -port <port>]
                      [-alternateserverlist -server <server name>
                           -host <server> -port <port>]
                      [-affinitylist -list <listname>
                           -serverorder "<server name1, server name2>"]
                      [-clientaffinitydefined -client <client name>
                           -host <server> -list <list name>]
                      [-clientaffinityroundrobin -client <client name>
                           -host <server>]
                   ]
                 ]
               } |
        remove { [ [-dsn <dsn_name>]
                   [-database <dbname> -host <server> -port <port>]
                 ],
                 [ [ [-parameter[s] "<par1>[;...;<parN>]"]
                     [-sessionglobalvariables "<par1>[;...;<parN>]"]
                     [-specialregisters "<par1>[;...;<parN>]"]
                     [-wlb "[<par1>;...;<parN>]"]
                     [-acr "[<par1>;...;<parN>]"
                        [-alternategroup "[<par1>;...;<parN>]"
                                         [-database <dbname>
                                          -host <server>
                                          -port <port>]]
                        [-alternateserverlist [-server <server name>]]
                        [-affinitylist [-list <listname>]]
                        [-clientaffinitydefined [-client <client name>]]
                        [-clientaffinityroundrobin [-client <client name>]]
                     ]
                   ] |
                   [-parameters]
                 ]
               } |
        -help
      }

Command parameters

  add

      Add dsn, database, parameter, session global variables, special register
      entries, wlb paremeters,and acr parameters and subsections like
      alternategroup, alternateserverlist, affinitylist, clientaffinitydefined
      & clientaffinityroundrobin entries to db2dsdriver.cfg

  remove

      Remove dsn, database, parameter, session global variables,special
      register  entries from db2dsdriver.cfg.

      If -dsn is specified, parameters/session global variables/special
      registers from matching dsn section are removed.

      If -database is specified, parameters/session global variables/special
      registers/wlb/acr parameters from matching database section are removed.

      If no <parameter>/<sessionglobalvariables> specified, the entire
      dsn/database section is removed.

      If no -dsn nor -database specified, parameters/session global variables
      are removed from GLOBAL section.

  -dsn <dsn_name> -description <dsn_description> -database <dbname> -host <server> -port <port>

      It specifies an alias name along with an optional description value.
      -dsn <dsn_name> mandatory for -description <dsn_description>.
      If -database is not specified <dsn_name> must exist in the
      db2dsdriver.cfg.

  -database <dbname> -host <server> -port <port>

      New database section will be created. The specified <parameter>/
      <sessionglobalvariables>/ <specialregisters>/ <wlb>/ <acr> and its
      subsectionsvalues will be added to the <database> section.

  -parameter[s] "<par1>=[<val1>];<par2>=[<val2>];...;<parN>=[<valN>]"

      Specifies parameter name to be added/removed from appropriate section of
      db2dsdriver.cfg.

      If "remove" option is specified and <parN> doesn't exist then no action
      will be taken.

      If "add" option is specified and <parN> already exists the current value
      will be overwritten with that specified in the <varN>

  -sessionglobalvariables "<par1>=[<val1>];<par2>=[<val2>];...;<parN>=[<valN>]"

      Specifies session global variable name to be added/removed from
      appropriate section of db2dsdriver.cfg.

      If "remove" option is specified and <parN> doesn't exist then no action
      will be taken.

      If "add" option is specified and <parN> already exists the current value
      will be overwritten with that specified in the <varN>

  -specialregisters "<par1>=[<val1>];<par2>=[<val2>];...;<parN>=[<valN>]"

      Specifies special register name to be added/removed from appropriate
      section of db2dsdriver.cfg.

      If "remove" option is specified and <parN> doesn't exist then no action
      will be taken.

      If "add" option is specified and <parN> already exists the current value
      will be overwritten with that specified in the <varN>

  -wlb "<par1>=[<val1>];...;<parN>=[<valN>];"

      Specifies workload balancing parameters to be added/removed from
      appropriate section of db2dsdriver.cfg.

      If "remove" option is specified and <parN> doesn't exist then no action
      will be taken.

      If "add" option is specified and <parN> already exists the current value
      will be overwritten with that specified in the <varN>

  -acr "<par1>=[<val1>];...;<parN>=[<valN>];"

      Specifies automatic client reroute parameters to be added/removed from
      appropriate section of db2dsdriver.cfg.

      If "remove" option is specified and <parN> doesn't exist then no action
      will be taken.

      If "add" option is specified and <parN> already exists the current value
      will be overwritten with that specified in the <varN>

  -alternategroup "[<par1>=<val1>;...;<parN>=<valN>;" [-database <dbname> -host <server> -port <port>]

      Specifies alternategroup parameters or database to be added/removed  from
      acr section of db2dsdriver.cfg.

      If "remove" option is specified and <parN> or database doesn't exist then
      no action will be taken.

      If "add" option is specified and <parN> already exists the current value
      will be overwritten with that specified in the <varN> and if database
      name with specific host, port trying to add already exist then no action
      will be taken

  -alternateserverlist [-server <server name> -host <server> -port <port>]

      Specifies alternateserverlist to be added/removed from acr section  of
      db2dsdriver.cfg.

      If "remove" option is specified and server doesn't exist then no action
      will be taken.

      If "add" option is specified and if server name with specific host and
      port is already configured  then no action will be taken

  -affinitylist [-list <list name> -serverorder "<server name1, server name2>"]

      Specifies affinitylist to be added/removed from acr section of
      db2dsdriver.cfg.

      If "remove" option is specified and list name doesn't exist then no
      action will be taken.

      If "add" option is specified and if list name with specific server order
      is already configured then no action will be taken

  -clientaffinitydefined [-client <client name> -host <server> -list <list name>]

      Specifies clientaffinitydefined to be added/removed from acr section of
      db2dsdriver.cfg.

      If "remove" option is specified and client name doesn't exist then no
      action will be taken.

      If "add" option is specified and if client name with specific host and
      list name is already configured then no action will be taken

  -clientaffinityroundrobin [-client <client name> -host <server>]

      Specifies clientaffinityroundrobin to be added/removed from acr section
      of db2dsdriver.cfg.

      If "remove" option is specified and client name doesn't exist then no
      action will be taken.

      If "add" option is specified and if client name with specific host is
      already configured then no action will be taken

  -help

      Display db2cli writecfg command help and usage information.